Reason: Let a module have a new instance load its grids and navmesh tiles as players reach them, as an open-world map does, instead of all at creation (a rift open loaded every grid on the world thread, over 30 s under load, and the freeze detector killed the server).
Target: AzerothCore at core-commit.txt, after patches 0001-0024 (0025 shares no file context). Default: stock, every grid of an instance loads when it is created.

--- a/src/server/game/Maps/Map.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Maps/Map.cpp
@@ -97,8 +97,9 @@
 // Hook called after map is created AND after added to map list
 void Map::OnCreateMap()
 {
-    // Instances load all grids by default (both base map and child maps)
-    if (GetInstanceId())
+    // Instances load all grids by default (both base map and child maps), unless a module has the instance load each grid
+    // as players reach it, as an open-world map does (a rift's)
+    if (GetInstanceId() && !sScriptMgr->IsInstanceLoadedOnDemand(this))
         LoadAllGrids();
 
     sScriptMgr->OnCreateMap(this);
